156
05:11:55,460 --> 05:12:10,750
Atty. Erwin G. Matib: Your Honor, before we proceed, I'd like to sincerely apologize to the presiding officer and to all the senator judges, as well as to our defense counsel and to our witness who has been waiting. to testify today.

157
05:12:12,310 --> 05:12:22,810
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Noted counsel and as the chair said earlier, let nothing further be said on the matter so that we don't I don't want to use the word waste but so that we don't spend time.

158
05:12:28,020 --> 05:12:38,180
Atty. Kristine R. Ferrer: Before we proceed with the examination of the witness of the prosecution, Your Honor, the defense would like to tackle some matters.

159
05:12:38,620 --> 05:12:39,300
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Of course, ma'am.

160
05:12:39,400 --> 05:13:15,480
Atty. Kristine R. Ferrer: First, Your Honor, in participating in the examination of this witness, the defendant is not waiving her right to question the legality of the submission of the tax returns before this honorable court. And second, the respondent requests, Your Honor, that through this honorable court, Your Honor, to direct the prosecution not to flash on screen copies of the tax returns and the relevant summaries for the following reasons.

161
05:13:15,480 --> 05:15:44,620
Atty. Kristine R. Ferrer: First, Your Honor, under Section 3, Subparagraph or Paragraph L, Subparagraph 3 of the Data Privacy Act. Tax returns are considered as sensitive personal information and they are considered as privilege and their publication shall be prohibited. And our second ground for the request, Your Honor, is that while the Office of the President through the Acting Secretary Executive Secretary authorized the submission of the tax returns before this honorable impeachment court through his memorandum dated July 29, 2026. Such authorization, Your Honor, does not include the inspection and viewing of the tax returns by the public. In fact, if I can quote the Executive Secretary's Memorandum. It says that you are hereby authorized to allow the inspection of and furnish the Senate Impeachment Court with one original or certified true copy accompanied by electronic copies contained in a USB flash drive including system-generated records. So if we peruse such memorandum from the acting Executive Secretary, Your Honor, the authorization or the Office of the President rather, the authorization is only limited or given to the Senate Impeachment Court to inspection or to inspect or view the tax returns in accordance with Section 71 of the National Internal Revenue Code, Your Honor. It is our position, Your Honor, that it is always better to err in favor of caution, Your Honor. That's why we request that if there are documents, Your Honor, that the Honorable judges need to peruse your honor or summaries or returns. Copies thereof should instead be provided to the honorable senator judges your honor for their reference instead of flashing them on the screen. Of course, there are certain things that we can allow such as provisions of law but when it comes to the income tax returns, VAT returns under summaries your honor, we beg this honorable court not to allow their display on screen your honor for the grounds that were Thank you.

162
05:15:45,960 --> 05:15:47,300
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Comment, Attorney Erwin?

163
05:15:49,670 --> 05:16:47,850
Atty. Erwin G. Matib: Your Honor, this is essentially a motion for reconsideration on a previous ruling of the impeachment court. The impeachment court already ruled that Section 16B of the Data Privacy Act as well as Section 22F of the Implementing Rules and Regulations of the DPA cover The records that we were, that we subpoenaed and which was granted by the Honorable Court. So this is essentially an MR on that ruling, Your Honor. And Your Honor, we should be able to show the tax returns precisely to prove the contents of The same, Your Honor. It would be useless for us to have the records without showing it to the Impeachment Court and to the public, Your Honor.

164
05:16:48,930 --> 05:16:50,170
Atty. Kristine R. Ferrer: Quick reply, Your Honor.

165
05:16:53,420 --> 05:16:55,120
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Yes, Attorney Kristine.

166
05:16:55,540 --> 05:17:25,370
Atty. Kristine R. Ferrer: Your Honor, we're not talking about the subpoena here because clearly the subpoena... Order the submission of these tax returns before the impeachment court. What we are asking the court is the flashing of the tax returns so that they can be viewed by the public. Again, if we peruse the memorandum that was issued by the Office of the President through the Executive Secretary, it is only the honorable impeachment court that was given the authority.

167
05:17:27,000 --> 05:17:41,960
Atty. Kristine R. Ferrer: The authority that was given to the CIR was to submit these tax returns in order for the impeachment court to view and examine them, Your Honor. It was not mentioned that it is for the viewing and examination of the public, Your Honor. Respectfully. Thank you.

168
05:17:42,900 --> 05:17:45,220
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Counsel, anything else you want to add?

169
05:17:45,440 --> 05:17:52,840
Atty. Erwin G. Matib: Your Honor, we have redacted certain personal information in the tax returns. We will not be showing addresses or even

170
05:17:54,450 --> 05:18:11,190
Atty. Erwin G. Matib: Names have nothing to do with respondent or her husband, Your Honor. We'll be showing amounts. We will not be showing even the tax identification number. We were able to redact all these sensitive personal information. So there's nothing for the defense to worry about, Your Honor.

171
05:18:11,410 --> 05:18:18,850
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Let's cross the bridge when we get there, counsel. Some attorney Erwin has not yet presented anything as of this moment. Should...

172
05:18:41,000 --> 05:18:42,880
Atty. Erwin G. Matib: Magandang hapon sa ating lahat.

173
05:18:44,640 --> 05:19:11,410
Atty. Erwin G. Matib: Ang testimonya ni Atty. Anne Loraine C. Garcia-Marquez ng Bureau of Internal Revenue ay magpapatunay sa mga sumusunod. Una, hindi tugma ang income ni VP Sara at ng kanyang asawa sa kanilang declared net worth. Base sa records ng BIR, 85.4 million ang kanilang kabuuwang net income mula 2007 hanggang 2025.

174
05:19:13,130 --> 05:20:03,670
Atty. Erwin G. Matib: Hindi nito maipaliwanag ang pagtaas ng net worth na umabot ng 98 million pesos sa pinakahuling SALN ni VP Sara. Pangalawa, nilabag ni VP Sara ang Constitution. Base sa records ng BIR, si VP Sara ay nagpractice ng kanyang profession at nakatanggap ng professional legal fees at iba pang kita. Maliban sa kanyang sahod bilang vicepresidente. Pangatlo, si VP Sara ay may undeclared cash at iba pang assets. Batay sa kanilang audited financial statements, ang mag-asawang VP Sara at Atty. Carpio ay may cash balances na P21M para sa taong 2022.

175
05:20:05,770 --> 05:20:08,830
Atty. Erwin G. Matib: P28M para sa taong 2023.

176
05:20:10,380 --> 05:20:59,240
Atty. Erwin G. Matib: 15 million pesos para sa taong 2024 at 13 million para sa taong 2025. Pang-apat, patungkol sa Cali88 Foods Corporation, base sa record ng BIR, patuloy na pag-aari ito ng Cali88 ng asawa ni VP Sara na si Atty. Manases Carpio. Sa madaling salita, Ang testigo ay magpapakita ng mga hindi na ideklarang income at iba pang assets, mga pagkakaiba sa pagitan ng tax records at mga SALN, at mga business interests at transaction na nangangailangan ng paliwanag. Sa kabuoan, ang mga ito ay may kaugnayan sa mga paglabag na nabanggit sa Article 2.

177
05:21:07,150 --> 05:21:09,730
Atty. Erwin G. Matib: That's all for my offer of testimony, Your Honor.

178
05:21:09,790 --> 05:21:11,330
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Comment, Atty. Kristine?

179
05:21:11,970 --> 05:21:14,010
Atty. Kristine R. Ferrer: Subject to cross-examination, Your Honor.

180
05:21:16,950 --> 05:21:19,610
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Noted. Proceed with your direct examination, Atty. Erwin.

181
05:21:21,510 --> 05:21:23,350
Atty. Erwin G. Matib: Good afternoon, Atty. Anne.

182
05:21:24,180 --> 05:21:25,260
Atty. Anne Loraine Garcia-Marquez: Good afternoon, po.

183
05:21:25,560 --> 05:21:26,980
Atty. Erwin G. Matib: Kumusta po kayo ngayong araw?

184
05:21:27,810 --> 05:21:28,730
Atty. Anne Loraine Garcia-Marquez: Okay naman po.

185
05:21:29,650 --> 05:21:39,870
Atty. Erwin G. Matib: So may tubig po dyan. Uminom lang kayo kung kinakailangan. So umpisa na natin ang pagtatanong. Ano ang inyong pangalan at ang inyong current na posisyon o trabaho?

186
05:21:41,390 --> 05:21:50,410
Atty. Anne Loraine Garcia-Marquez: Ako po si Atty. Anne Loraine Garcia-Marquez. Ako po ang Chief of Staff ni Commissioner Charlito Martin R. Mendoza.

187
05:21:51,290 --> 05:21:59,290
Atty. Erwin G. Matib: At ano pong mga posisyon niyo kung mayroon man sa BIR bago kayo naging Chief of Staff?

188
05:22:00,970 --> 05:22:23,340
Atty. Anne Loraine Garcia-Marquez: Before po ako naging Chief of Staff, nung pumasok po ako sa BIR, ako po ay naging Action Lawyer sa Legal and Legislative Division. Tapos po, ako naman po ay naging Chief of Staff ng Office of the Deputy Commissioner for Legal Group. And then ngayon po, ako naman po ngayon ang Chief of Staff ng Commissioner of Internal Revenue.

189
05:22:24,100 --> 05:22:26,940
Atty. Erwin G. Matib: At ano ang inyong mga kursong tinapos?

190
05:22:30,080 --> 05:22:41,160
Atty. Anne Loraine Garcia-Marquez: Ako po ay nagtapos ng BS in Business Administration and Accountancy. At I earned my Juris Doctor degree sa Ateneo de Manila University School of Law.

191
05:22:42,760 --> 05:22:43,760
Atty. Erwin G. Matib: UPBAA kayo?

192
05:22:44,750 --> 05:22:45,390
Atty. Anne Loraine Garcia-Marquez: Tama po.

193
05:22:45,510 --> 05:22:47,050
Atty. Erwin G. Matib: Ito po ay quota course, tama?

194
05:22:47,550 --> 05:22:48,270
Atty. Anne Loraine Garcia-Marquez: Tama po.

195
05:22:49,880 --> 05:22:52,160
Atty. Erwin G. Matib: Ano naman ang inyong mga profesyon?

196
05:22:54,750 --> 05:22:58,550
Atty. Anne Loraine Garcia-Marquez: Ako po ay isang certified public accountant and ako rin po ay isang lawyer.

197
05:22:59,800 --> 05:23:03,460
Atty. Erwin G. Matib: Ano ang inyong work experience bago pumasok sa BIR, kung mayroon man?

198
05:23:05,120 --> 05:23:21,480
Atty. Anne Loraine Garcia-Marquez: Bago po pumasok ng BIR, ako po ay nag-work sa isang audit firm. Tapos after po nun ay nag-work din po ako sa isang law firm and then Nag-in-house counsel din po ako sa isang private company bago po ako pumasok ng BIR.

199
05:23:21,840 --> 05:23:31,800
Atty. Erwin G. Matib: Thank you. Balikan natin yung position mo bilang Chief of Staff ng Commissioner of Internal Revenue. Anong inyong duties and responsibilities as Chief of Staff?

200
05:23:33,460 --> 05:23:55,830
Atty. Anne Loraine Garcia-Marquez: As Chief of Staff, ako po ay tumutulong sa daily operations ng Office of the Commissioner. And nagre-review din po ako ng mga documents and lahat po nang sinasign ng Commissioner of Internal Revenue. And naka-receive din po ako ng lahat ng mga letters and correspondences for the Commissioner of Internal Revenue.

201
05:23:56,820 --> 05:23:59,500
Atty. Erwin G. Matib: Bakit kayo nandito ngayon sa impeachment court?

202
05:24:00,750 --> 05:24:10,870
Atty. Anne Loraine Garcia-Marquez: Naka-receive po ako ng subpoena from the Senate Impeachment Court to attend yung trial po for yesterday and today po.

203
05:24:11,500 --> 05:24:19,160
Atty. Erwin G. Matib: At tama ba na bago nyo natanggap itong sapina na ito, may natanggap din kayong isa pang sapina para mag-submit ng mga documents sa impeachment court?

204
05:24:19,790 --> 05:24:20,650
Atty. Anne Loraine Garcia-Marquez: Tama po.

205
05:24:21,310 --> 05:24:26,050
Atty. Erwin G. Matib: At ano ang inyong mga sinubmit na documents para maka-comply sa sapina?

206
05:24:28,970 --> 05:24:39,210
Atty. Anne Loraine Garcia-Marquez: Lahat po nung tax records and information na nakalagay sa sapina, yun po yung lahat nung sinubmit po namin sa Senate Impeachment Court.

207
05:24:41,080 --> 05:24:43,260
Atty. Erwin G. Matib: Kaninong records itong mga ito?

208
05:24:44,560 --> 05:24:53,980
Atty. Anne Loraine Garcia-Marquez: Records po ni Vice President Sara Duterte, her spouse, attorney Manases R. Carpio, and other identified business entities.

209
05:24:54,460 --> 05:25:18,140
Atty. Erwin G. Matib: Your Honor, we invoke the earlier ruling of the presiding officer that the BIR records are public records which are self-authenticating. These were submitted by the BIR directly to the court and not the parties so there is no doubt as to the chain of custody of these documents and therefore we'll no longer... Have the witness authenticate or identify all these documents.

210
05:25:19,000 --> 05:25:20,040
Atty. Kristine R. Ferrer: Comment, Your Honor.

211
05:25:20,870 --> 05:25:22,130
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Comment, Attorney Kristine.

212
05:25:22,490 --> 05:25:44,920
Atty. Kristine R. Ferrer: Your Honor, there was no ruling that those are considered already as public documents. In fact, by their very nature, the tax returns are considered as private documents. What the... What the impeachment court only ordered was the reproduction of the tax returns before this honorable court, not the conversion of those documents into public records, Your Honor. Thank you.

213
05:25:44,960 --> 05:25:52,140
